cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you report energy measured with joules in a paper, please cite it like this."
title: "joules: like time, but for energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Bharat
    affiliation: "PHENEX TECHNOLOGIES INC. (WattOps)"
version: 0.8.2
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: MIT
url: "https://wattops.dev/joules"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/landauer-gap/"
abstract: >-
  joules measures the energy of any command, local model or phase of a program from the hardware's own
  counters: NVML for NVIDIA GPUs, RAPL for Intel and AMD CPUs and DRAM, amdgpu and Intel GPU hwmon, and
  powermetrics on Macs. It records clocks, throttling, temperature and power limits with every result, and
  compares two ways of doing the same work with interleaved runs, medians and a Mann-Whitney test.
keywords:
  - energy measurement
  - GPU
  - RAPL
  - NVML
  - green AI
  - benchmarking
